Nope, converging after 1 iterations is likely due to the simplicity of the model (it is a linear regression model). Your code looks (mostly) correct. I think the + 0 at the end of the first line might be causing some problems (and it isn't affecting the model). You've specified the inequality constraint correctly, but you'll notice that the Slack for the inequality constrain is not close to 0 (Slack = 0 is a binding constraint, non 0 Slack means a constraint is either non-binding or impossible given the data).

